Subject: drivers: i2c: stm32_v2: handle controller/target own-address races

Backport the upstream STM32 v2 combined controller/target race handling onto
the pinned Zephyr 4.4.1 release. This is the minimal functional series from:

  dd9b1122e10 drivers: i2c: stm32_v2: abort pending controller START on ADDR
  879678acbb9 drivers: i2c: stm32_v2: handle controller/target own-address races
  a1609f6a45a drivers: i2c: stm32_v2: make target preempt check explicit

The local backport also carries the later upstream CONFIG_I2C_TARGET guard for
wait_bus_idle() so non-target builds do not warn about an unused helper.

Without this series, an own-address match can arrive while the peripheral is
starting a controller transfer. The 4.4.1 driver stays on the controller path,
blocks target IRQ handling, and can wedge.

Separately, HIL reproduced KERNEL_PANIC in i2c_stm32_target_event() when the
previous application recovery briefly unregistered the target. Keep the target
registered continuously because an external controller may address the DUT at
any time. Applied automatically by Firmware/CMakeLists.txt.

